    <section class="shell section"><div class="section-head"><div class="section-index">01 / FOUNDRY</div><div class="section-title"><h2>Move from a prompt to an operable system.</h2><p>Design the identity, model, tools, knowledge, output contract, and evaluation criteria together—then manage versions deliberately.</p></div></div><div class="grid-2"><article class="card"><div class="icon-box">AF</div><h3>AI Agent Foundry</h3><p>Create, test, publish, deprecate, and disable versioned agent definitions with a visible lifecycle and immutable published versions.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="icon-box">PL</div><h3>Pipelines</h3><p>Combine model calls, deterministic steps, tools, validations, and handoffs into an explicit execution path.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="icon-box">GR</div><h3>Guardrails</h3><p>Constrain tools and data access, validate structured outputs, apply policy checks, and route sensitive changes for approval.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="icon-box">MR</div><h3>Memory &amp; RAG</h3><p>Ground responses in selected records and knowledge sources while keeping retrieval scope attached to the agent's effective access.</p></article></div></section>
